# signatures.db - ALmap v3.0 default service signature database.
# Format: TYPE|<port_or_any>|<pattern_to_match>|<service_name>
# - TYPE is EXACT (literal substring) or REGEX (POSIX extended regex).
# - Blank lines and lines starting with # are ignored.
# - <port_or_any> is "any" or a port 1..65535.
# - Patterns are 1..255 bytes and may contain '|'; the last '|'
#   separator ends the pattern.
# - <service_name> is printable ASCII without '|' or spaces.
# - First match wins, in file order. Invalid lines are skipped.
# Install a custom database at ~/.almap/signatures.db (the default
# lookup path) or pass --sigdb <path> with --service.
# MySQL is not expressible as a portable text signature (its signature
# is the protocol byte 10 at offset 4) so it stays hardcoded in
# modules/service.goose.
# tools/import_nmap.py converts nmap-service-probes into this format.

EXACT|80|Server:|http
EXACT|8080|Server:|http
EXACT|8000|Server:|http
REGEX|any|^SSH-[0-9]+\.[0-9]+-|ssh
EXACT|any|SMTP|smtp
EXACT|any|220|ftp
